{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-09 19:53 PST\n\nSession a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d stopped at a clean point. Nothing of this session is running: no gate op, no make verify, no CI poll.\n\n## Children (dependency order; each depends_on the previous unless noted)\n1. polonium-autophobic-anchovy (0f4c-4586-8f3e-432d), ADR: CLOSED. Plan review PASS (signed); completion-verifier close passed 2026-11-09 ~19:10 PST.\n2. maize-guilty-hapuku (3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab), reducer/RELEASE_DELTA/SCHEMA_VERSION 6: OPEN, unclaimed. Plan review PASS, signed 19:52 PST at main 06b3b1a5230 (third revision of the plan; it now includes the _REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION 8->9 bump). No code written.\n3. lovely-bipartisan-mullet (50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac), inbound: OPEN. Not reviewed (blocked by #2; review-plan fast-fails INDETERMINATE until #2 closes).\n4. volcanic-prim-parakeet (59f4-6a6f-71e5-4084), outbound: OPEN. Not reviewed (blocked by #3).\n5. gymnasial-snappy-lorikeet (ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50), missing/archived-version alerts: OPEN. Not reviewed (blocked by #4).\n6. waiting-nonspinal-ermine (15e2-68c2-fab2-4cbd), surfaces and docs: OPEN. Not reviewed. Depends on #4 and #5 (#5 edge added for the shared docs/jira-sync-setup.md).\n7. plucky-jetblack-parrot (80c7-7d3a-158e-4845), production round trip [non-codebase]: OPEN. Not reviewed. Depends on #5 and #6.\nEpic inferior-seaborgium-aruanas: IN_PROGRESS; plan review PASS (signed at 872e7f6c3fd).\n\n## Gerrit changes\n- 3337 \"Record the fix-versions release design (ADR 0124)\": MERGED as 49f5d6d05802552fc656b53c9a0b3ed661ff89da (patch set 3, Gerrit's server-side rebase of ps2 b8852268fd7). LLM-Review +1, Verified +1. Not WIP.\n- 3338 (another session's ADR 0123, selectable plan-review engine): MERGED as a7e6fb56209. Listed only because it shares the README index; no action needed.\n- No other open changes from this session.\n\n## Worktrees\n- /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/fixver-epic, branch fixver-epic, at origin/main 06b3b1a5230, clean (no tracked changes). Installed with make install at rebar 0.15.0. Scratch (git-ignored): .rebar/scratch/a85e3cd3-plans/ holds the child plan sources c1-c7*.md (c2-reducer.md is the current #2 plan), review logs rp-*.log, and make-verify-c1*.log.\n- /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.rebar/worktrees/fix-bridge-lockblob was used only to run ticket CLI writes while make verify occupied fixver-epic; it holds no work for this epic.\n- MCP rebar tools were unavailable in this session; all tracker ops used the worktree's .venv/bin/rebar.\n\n## Next steps, in order\n1. In fixver-epic: git fetch origin && git merge --ff-only origin/main; run make install if main crossed a version bump. Gates read model config from origin/main but run local code; a stale install fails them (bug misogynic-scheelite-solitaire).\n2. Check the #2 attestation is still current: rebar review-plan maize-guilty-hapuku --status. If stale (main moved), re-run review-plan.\n3. rebar claim maize-guilty-hapuku (no --assignee). Implement per its plan (Approach steps 1-9: _version.py RELEASE_DELTA + KNOWN_EVENT_TYPES + SCHEMA_VERSION 6; shared _fold_list_delta + process_release_delta in _processors.py; _replay.py dispatch; \"releases\": [] in _state.py; _cache.py version 9; event_prepare.py allow-list + message; fsck_repair.py _AUTO_RECOVER_ORPHAN_TYPES; ticket_state.schema.json + regenerate types.py; docs/event-schema.md row + v6 history) with the tests listed in its Testing section.\n4. Commit with \"rebar-ticket: 3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab\" and git commit -s (subject <= 50 chars, body wrapped at 72; the hook enforces it). Run env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify with no timeout (55-78 min on this host). Push: git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main%hashtag=rebar-session-<id> (WIP is no longer required). Land at LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved with scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py <n> --revision <full sha>. Fast-forward the worktree, tick the ACs, then close (completion-verifier gate). Note: editing a description after review (even to tick boxes) can trip the close gate's stale-material check; ticking alone is attestation-safe, but any text change needs a fresh review-plan first.\n5. Repeat for #3, #4, #5, #6 in order. Re-check each plan's line citations against current main before review.\n6. #7: bring the REB admin prerequisite to the coordinator before starting (see Open items).\n\n## Decisions made (do not reopen)\n- Releases set from rebar keep the labels behavior exactly as ADR 0124 records it (coordinator 2026-11-09). A Jira-side rename of such a release leaves the rebar ticket with both names plus a BRIDGE_ALERT naming the old one.\n- Archived versions are withheld from outbound adds and get their own alert reason, release-version-archived:<name>.\n- A failed version-list read raises no alert and resolves none (availability unknown for that project and pass).\n- The ADR is number 0124 (0123 belongs to the selectable plan-review engine ADR, ticket 11f7-cf57-be02-4441).\n- Carrier: a new RELEASE_DELTA event, not a TAG_DELTA field selector.\n\n## Open items\n- #7 needs a Jira admin, before it starts, to create one version in project REB (e.g. rebar-fixver-probe), and possibly to add Fix versions to REB's edit screen. ADR 0124's Evidence records that Jira's edit endpoint documentation says it does not check screen configuration, contradicting the screen prerequisite; #7 settles it live. Sessions must not write to REB themselves.\n- Bug misogynic-scheelite-solitaire (ac3b-c6cd-8076-4a98), filed discovered_from #2: gates read model config from origin/main but run local code, so a stale worktree install fails gates with an opaque provider 400. Not being worked on.\n- Not investigated: the reconcile-bridge.yml run 42674086557 failure at 10:26 PST (GitHub: workflow file issue); later runs succeeded."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794282846308247001,"uuid":"c07714d3-8f9f-4373-824b-c9f0654c0050"}